<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia's Telstra year net rises 31.5 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia's Telstra year net rises 31.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit (billion)	 3.24 vs 2.97</p>
<p>    Net (billion)			  2.30 vs 1.75</p>
<p>    Abnormal profit		     204.6 vs loss 567.8</p>
<p>NOTE: Telecommunications carrier Telstra Corporation Ltd is owned by the Australian government.  </p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	     10.6 vs 8.3</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	     21.3 vs 14.7</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date Dec 31</p>
<p>Reg date not applicable</p>
<p>    Sales (billion)		     14.72 vs 13.61</p>
<p>    Other income			  522.2 vs 468.3</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				36 vs 27</p>
<p>    Tax				   1,144.6 vs 649.6</p>
<p>    Interest				553.0 vs 506.4</p>
<p>    Depreciation (billion)	     2.32 vs 2.18</p>
<p>    Minorities			 gain 2.6 vs charge 2.7</p>
<p>NOTE: Telstra said the abnormal profit reflected change in communications assets depreciation methodology.</p>
<p>Telstra said the net tangible asset backing per share was A$1.77 in 1995/96 vs A$1.57 per share in 1994/95.</p>
<p>The Australian government plans to sell one-third of Telstra in the 1997/98 year.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 973 1800</p>
</text>
